{"id": "DezEwkNxDAi", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why are Hindu gods BLUE? 💙 The answer was hiding in their names all along… and Shiva isn't blue at all 🤯\n\n🔵 Krishna literally means \"dark\" (Sanskrit kṛṣṇa). That's why he's also called Ghanshyam: dark as a rain cloud.\n🪷 Tulsidas sings of Shri Ram as \"nīlāmbuja-śyāmala\": dark as a blue lotus (Ramcharitmanas, Ayodhya Kand).\n☁️ The Vishnu shloka you hear at home, Shantakaram, calls him \"megha-varnam\": the colour of a cloud.\n🎨 Dark as a monsoon sky. So in paintings, that dark became blue.\n\nBut here's the twist 👇\n⚪ Shiva is \"Karpur Gauram\": white as camphor. You sing it after every aarti!\n💙 Only his throat is blue: he held the Halahala poison there to save the world. That's why he's Neelkanth (Bhagavata Purana 8.7).\n\nYour child will ask you this one day. Now you know 🙏\n\n📚 Rishi Katha picture books tell our gods' stories for kids, in simple words and bright pictures. 15K FAMILY DEAL: Books 1–3 for ₹350 (was ₹500), only till 25 Oct midnight. Comment FAMILY and we'll DM you the deal, or tap the link in bio → rishikatha.com\n\n💬 Did YOU know Shiva was white? Comment YES or NO!\n🔖 Save this for the next time your kid asks, and share it with someone who sings Karpur Gauram every evening.\n\n#krishna #shiva #ram #vishnu #hindugods #karpurgauram #neelkanth #ghanshyam #sanatandharma #hindumythology #indianmythology #kidsbooks #rishikatha #mythologyforkids #hinduism", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792675292, "like_count": 37305, "comment_count": 249, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-3328051537395075a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 53.335, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQPX9piR94Monk6hyP5t_Wz9fy4keB6Zg1ElQjp7p_axbJ-1oX3fc6EuadHAV5HU